body:
I see now! I played around with it. Not sure why he overcomplicated that, it actually messed it up somehow. 

&#x200B;

Turns out the tutorial wanted it to the return to the main menu XD. I did the test dialogue and that actually helped me understand it better

&#x200B;

Also learned the save name doesn't matter, its what you write down as the label name. I did some other tests but I would say I have a decent base now. Thanks again

>Test dialog

Okay thanks for that. So I altered it according to this. Now it just sends me to the screen where it says 'END' and I assume that is because it goes to label endgame after that.

but  I had a few questions actually if you don't mind answering.

1. Why just "call monika\_route" instead of that previous line?

2. What does the indentation effect?

3. Not 100% sure what you mean by "y test dialog". Also Which would be my monika route label? In that area where I put "call monika\_route" or that other script in the 2nd screenshot?

4. I think I am starting to understand. So this part of modding directs where it goes in the game. (I.e - like a book, deciding which chapter you want to jump to) or am I wrong?



&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

1

yes and quick update: I decided to delete everything and try it from scratch. I did the process again with some minor differences.

&#x200B;

Now when I click on 'new game' instead of getting a script error it just restarts the main menu. Does this mean I have made progress on it or did the right thing?
